<Base lang="en" title="Caldrew | Legal" description="Privacy policy, terms and conditions, and cookie policy for the Caldrew website.">
<section id="privacy" class="cd-legal"><div class="cd-legal-container"><p class="cd-eyebrow">Caldrew</p><h1 class="cd-legal-title">Privacy Policy</h1><p class="cd-legal-updated">Last updated: 22 July 2026</p><hr class="cd-legal-divider cd-legal-divider"/><p class="cd-legal-lede">This Privacy Policy explains how Caldrew collects and processes personal data when you visit this website or contact us through it. We collect and process only the personal data necessary to operate the site and respond to your enquiries.</p><h2 class="cd-h2">1. Who we are</h2><p class="cd-p"><strong>Data Controller: Caldrew, S.A.</strong>, registered at <strong>Rua Castilho, 32 - 4, 1250-070 Lisboa</strong>, Portugal, tax number (NIPC) <strong>519 415 949</strong>.</p><p class="cd-p"><strong>Contact for data protection matters: </strong><a href="mailto:enquiries@caldrew.com" class="cd-a">enquiries@caldrew.com</a></p><h2 class="cd-h2">2. What we collect</h2><ul role="list" class="cd-ul"><li class="cd-li"><strong>Contact form information.</strong> When you use the contact form we collect your name, email address and company, together with any message you send.</li><li class="cd-li"><strong>Technical information.</strong> Like any website, our hosting and security providers process limited technical data such as your IP address, browser type and the pages you visit. This is used to serve the site and protect it against abuse.</li></ul><p class="cd-p">We do not use advertising trackers, behavioral analytics, profiling or automated decision-making, and we do not knowingly collect personal data from individuals under the age of 18.</p><h2 class="cd-h2">3. Why we use it and our legal basis</h2><ul role="list" class="cd-ul"><li class="cd-li"><strong>To respond to your enquiry and manage our communications with you.</strong> Legal basis: our legitimate interest in answering you, or taking steps at your request before entering into a business relationship (Article 6(1)(f) and 6(1)(b) GDPR).</li><li class="cd-li"><strong>To operate, maintain and secure the website.</strong> Legal basis: our legitimate interest in ensuring that the website remains available, functional and protected against abuse (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR).</li></ul><h2 class="cd-h2">4. Who we share it with</h2><p class="cd-p">We do not sell your data. We rely on a small number of service providers who process data on our behalf under contract:</p><ul role="list" class="cd-ul"><li class="cd-li"><strong>Webflow, Inc.</strong> Website hosting and contact form processing.</li><li class="cd-li"><strong>Cloudflare, Inc.</strong> Security and bot protection for the form.</li><li class="cd-li"><strong>Google LLC.</strong> Provision of the fonts used on the website, which requires the transmission of your IP address to Google.</li></ul><p class="cd-p">Some of these providers are based in the United States. Where personal data is transferred outside the European Economic Area, such transfers are safeguarded through the European Commission&#x27;s Standard Contractual Clauses or another legally recognized transfer mechanism.</p><h2 class="cd-h2">5. How long we keep it</h2><p class="cd-p">We retain enquiry data for as long as necessary to respond to your request and for a reasonable period afterwards for record-keeping, after which it is securely deleted.</p><h2 class="cd-h2">6. Your rights</h2><p class="cd-p">You have the right to access your personal data, request its rectification or erasure, request restriction of processing, object to processing, request data portability, and withdraw your consent at any time where processing is based on consent. To exercise any of these rights, please contact us using the details provided in Section 1. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the Portuguese Supervisory Authority, the Comissão Nacional de Proteção de Dados (CNPD).</p><h2 class="cd-h2">7. Changes</h2><p class="cd-p">We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The current version and the date of its latest revision will always appear at the top of this section.</p></div></section><div><section id="terms" class="cd-legal"><div class="cd-legal-container"><hr class="cd-legal-divider cd-legal-divider"/><h1 class="cd-legal-title">Terms and Conditions</h1><p class="cd-legal-updated">Last updated: 22 July 2026</p><hr class="cd-legal-divider cd-legal-divider"/><p class="cd-legal-lede">These Terms and Conditions govern your use of the Caldrew website. By accessing or using this website, you agree to be bound by these Terms and Conditions.</p><p class="cd-p">The website is operated by <strong>Caldrew, S.A.</strong></p><h2 class="cd-h2">1. Purpose of the site</h2><p class="cd-p">This website is provided solely for general information about Caldrew and its activities. Nothing on this website is intended to constitute professional advice or create any contractual relationship.</p><h2 class="cd-h2">2. No offer and no advice</h2><p class="cd-p">Nothing on this website constitutes, or should be construed as, an offer, solicitation, recommendation or invitation to buy, sell or subscribe for any security, financial instrument or investment, nor does it constitute investment, legal, tax or financial advice.</p><p class="cd-p">The information published on this website is not directed at any person in any jurisdiction where its publication or use would be contrary to applicable law or regulation.</p><p class="cd-p">You should obtain independent professional advice before making any investment or other financial decision.</p><h2 class="cd-h2">3. Accuracy of content</h2><p class="cd-p">We take reasonable care to ensure that the content of this website is accurate and up to date.</p><p class="cd-p">However, we make no representation or warranty, express or implied, that the information is complete, accurate, current or free from errors.</p><p class="cd-p">The content may be amended, updated or removed at any time without notice, and it should not be relied upon as the sole basis for any decision.</p><h2 class="cd-h2">4. Intellectual property</h2><p class="cd-p">All content on this website, including text, logos, graphics, images, layout and design, is owned by Caldrew or its licensors and is protected by applicable intellectual property laws.</p><p class="cd-p">You may view, download and print this content solely for your personal, non-commercial use.</p><p class="cd-p">Any other use, including reproduction, modification, distribution or republication, requires our prior written consent.</p><h2 class="cd-h2">5. Third-party websites</h2><p class="cd-p">The website may contain links to third-party websites for your convenience.</p><p class="cd-p">We do not control those websites and accept no responsibility for their content, availability or privacy practices.</p><h2 class="cd-h2">6. Limitation of liability</h2><p class="cd-p">To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, Caldrew shall not be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental or consequential loss or damage arising out of, or in connection with, your use of, inability to use, or reliance upon this website or its content.</p><h2 class="cd-h2">7. Governing law</h2><p class="cd-p">These terms are governed by the laws of Portugal.</p><p class="cd-p">The Portuguese courts have exclusive jurisdiction over any dispute arising out of or in connection with this website or these Terms and Conditions.</p><h2 class="cd-h2">8. Contact</h2><p class="cd-p">Questions regarding these Terms and Conditions can be sent to <a href="mailto:enquiries@caldrew.com" class="cd-a">enquiries@caldrew.com</a>.</p></div></section><section id="cookies" class="cd-legal"><div class="cd-legal-container"><hr class="cd-legal-divider cd-legal-divider"/><h1 class="cd-legal-title">Cookie Policy</h1><p class="cd-legal-updated">Last updated: 22 July 2026</p><hr class="cd-legal-divider cd-legal-divider"/><p class="cd-legal-lede">This policy explains the cookies and similar technologies used on this website. We limit their use to those strictly necessary for the operation and security of the website.</p><h2 class="cd-h2">1. Our approach</h2><p class="cd-p">This website does not use analytics, advertising or profiling cookies. It does not set first-party tracking cookies.</p><p class="cd-p">We only use technologies that are strictly necessary to operate the website securely and protect the contact form against abuse.</p><p class="cd-p">Because these technologies are strictly necessary for the provision of the website, their use does not require user consent under applicable law.</p><h2 class="cd-h2">2. Technologies we use</h2><table class="cd-table cd-table"><thead><tr><th class="cd-th cd-th">Technology</th><th class="cd-th cd-th">Provider</th><th class="cd-th cd-th">Purpose</th><th class="cd-th cd-th">Type and duration</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="cd-td cd-td">Cloudflare Turnstile</td><td class="cd-td cd-td">Cloudflare, Inc.</td><td class="cd-td cd-td">Protects the contact form against bots and abuse. Runs a lightweight browser check when the form is used.</td><td class="cd-td cd-td">Strictly necessary (security). May place a short-lived challenge token. It is not used for cross-site tracking.</td></tr><tr><td class="cd-td cd-td">Webflow hosting</td><td class="cd-td cd-td">Webflow, Inc.</td><td class="cd-td cd-td">Serves and secures the website and processes contact form submissions.</td><td class="cd-td cd-td">Strictly necessary (technical). No advertising or profiling.</td></tr><tr><td class="cd-td cd-td">Google Fonts</td><td class="cd-td cd-td">Google LLC</td><td class="cd-td cd-td">Loads the typefaces used on the site so the pages render correctly.</td><td class="cd-td cd-td">No cookies are placed. Your IP address is transmitted to Google to serve the font files.</td></tr></tbody></table><p class="cd-note">Google Fonts sets no cookie, but loading the fonts from Google transmits your IP address to Google. This information is included here in the interest of transparency.</p><h2 class="cd-h2">3. Managing cookies</h2><p class="cd-p">You may block or delete cookies at any time through your browser settings.</p><p class="cd-p">Please note that disabling strictly necessary technologies may prevent parts of the website, particularly the contact form, from functioning correctly.</p><h2 class="cd-h2">4. Future changes</h2><p class="cd-p">If we introduce analytics, performance or marketing cookies in the future, we will request your consent through an appropriate cookie banner before such cookies are placed and we will update this Cookie Policy accordingly.</p></div></section></div>
